-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6 sm:p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How This Calculator Works\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Look at your pay stub sometime. That number at the bottom — the one that actually hits your bank — is way smaller than the number at the top. This calculator tells you why, line by line. All withholding calculations follow \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p15t\\\\\\\" target=\\\\\\\"_blank\\\\\\\" rel=\\\\\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\\\\\"\\u003eIRS Publication 15-T\\u003c/a\\u003e.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Here's what comes out of every paycheck. Federal tax uses progressive brackets from 10% up to 37%, with standard deductions of $16,100 (single) or $32,200 (married). Then \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/glossary\\\\\\\"\\u003eFICA\\u003c/a\\u003e: 6.2% for Social Security on income up to $184,500, and 1.45% for Medicare on everything. Make over $200,000? Add another 0.9% Medicare surtax on the amount above that.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"My buddy in Chicago and I compared stubs once. Same salary, same filing status. He walked away with about $3,800 less for the year because Illinois takes 4.95% and my state takes nothing. That's when it hit me — state tax is not a small factor. We cover five states here: Illinois at 4.95% flat, Texas at 0%, Florida at 0%, California at 1%–13.3% progressive, and New York at 4%–10.9% plus a potential NYC tax.\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"A couple things that help soften the blow:\\u003cbr/\\u003e- \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"/401k-retirement-calculator\\\\\\\"\\u003e401(k) contributions\\u003c/a\\u003e reduce taxable income at both federal and state level\\u003cbr/\\u003e- HSA contributions do the same\\u003cbr/\\u003e- These pre-tax deductions are basically a discount on your tax bill\\\"}}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\\\":{\\\"__html\\\":\\\"Bottom line — you'll see your net pay, effective tax rate, and marginal rate. Most people think their effective rate is higher than it actually is. Go ahead, see for yourself.\\\"}}]]}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6 sm:p-8\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How It's Calculated\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-5\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Formula\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/30 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-foreground\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Net Pay = Gross Income − (Federal Tax + State Tax + FICA + Pre-tax Deductions)\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Step-by-Step\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"ol\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"space-y-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"li\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"flex gap-3 